# adminui build-time configuration.
#
# There is deliberately almost nothing here, and no secret ever goes in this
# file. The API base URL is NOT a build-time value: it comes from
# /admin/env.json at runtime (WEB-2), which is what lets one image serve dev,
# staging and live without a rebuild. Anything in this file IS baked into the
# bundle and is therefore public.
#
# Copy to .env.local for local work. .env.local is git-ignored.
#
# Set it in .env.local rather than inline on the command line: npm runs scripts
# through cmd.exe on Windows, where `VITE_ENABLE_MOCK=1 npm run dev` is not a
# command. That is why this service has no `cross-env` dependency.

# Where `npm run dev` proxies /admin-auth and /api. This exists so the browser
# always sees a same-origin request in development, which keeps CORS out of the
# dev path entirely. It is empty in production because there the SPA is served
# by the same gateway_dev that serves the API.
#
# Default when unset: http://127.0.0.1:8090, gateway_dev's public listener
# (services/gateway_dev/testdata/manual/TESTING.md).
VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8090

# Set to 1 to serve the fixture API from MSW instead of proxying to a real
# gateway. Never set for a build: the mock is imported behind a build-time
# constant, so with this unset the branch and the whole mocks/ directory are
# dead-code-eliminated. The generated worker under mock/ is kept out of the
# image as well: .dockerignore excludes that directory from the build context.
VITE_ENABLE_MOCK=
